Unit support model (free support + city garrison)
=================================================

Context (2026-09)
-----------------
Late-game unit counts push the global u16 unit vector toward saturation. Aggregation
(notes.unit_size) shrinks field entity count. A second lever is Civ6-style city defense
so every city does not need a permanent mobile land unit parked as garrison.

Clarified support picture (three free-support kinds)
----------------------------------------------------
We keep free city support as it exists today and add city-bound garrison as a third
kind. Intended model:

1) Free civ-wide support
   Empire-level free support pool (existing civ/player free support concept).

2) Free city support while in city
   Existing per-city free land / free naval support for normal units that are
   currently in (or assigned to) that city — mobile units that can leave.

3) Free support for units bound permanently to the city
   New third support type for Civ6-style garrison: city-tied defense that does not
   leave the city (other than possibly striking units that surround / adjacent to
   the city). Consumes garrison support slots, not the mobile land support budget.

So: free city support for visitors/home mobile units stays; garrison is an additional
bucket for permanently city-bound defense, not a replacement for (1) or (2).

Why a third type
----------------
- Garrisons stop competing with field armies for land free-support.
- AI can fill garrison support via walls / city defense / bound garrison, and spend
  land support on aggregated attack stacks.
- Matches “city holds itself; field armies conquer.”

Design notes / open points
--------------------------
- Is (3) purely city HP + city strike (no UnitAdd entity), or a real unit flagged
  non-leaving that burns garrison support while in city?
- If both a mobile land unit and garrison exist in a city: land support vs garrison
  support ownership rules.
- Garrison free slots should scale slower than land free support so late cities are
  not invulnerable sponges.
- City attack vs adjacent besiegers needs enough teeth that AI/players do not still
  spam size-1 home guards.
- Existing heuristics that assume “units on city tile” / free land support for
  defense must be taught about garrison support and city combat.

Relationship to unit size
-------------------------
Aggregation (notes.unit_size) targets mobile combat mass. Garrison support targets
static home defense. Use both: do not rely on formations alone to clear city-guard
spam, and do not rely on city defense alone to shrink field doomstacks.
